# Review checklist

Judge the candidate rubric as a whole, with emphasis on the edited parts:

- clarity: each rule states one unambiguous judgment a judge can act on;

- atomicity: no "and"/"or" chains fusing several verdicts into one rule;

- judgeability: every rule can be verified from the trajectory alone,
  without external knowledge or unverifiable ceremony;

- coherence: no duplicated or mutually contradictory rules within a
  subcriterion; style and language (Chinese) consistent with the rubric;

- structure: each criterion keeps 1 to 5 subcriteria, each subcriterion
  keeps 1 to 5 rules; subcriterion ids remain unique and matched to their
  parent criterion; added subcriteria carry a name, a description and
  rule-complete definitions; the six A-F criteria themselves are untouched.

Minor stylistic imperfections are acceptable; a rule that would force a
judge to reason incorrectly, or an edit that breaks the structure above,
is not. Set quality_pass to false whenever adopting the candidate would
make the rubric systemically worse.

